# Goal
# Ordered ground waypoints to follow, normalized image space (point.x, point.y in
# [-1, 1], center = 0; z unused), nearest-first — the PlanVisualPath.markers layout.
# hint_navigation/path_projector grounds them into an odom nav_msgs/Path and drives
# Nav2's follow_path (MPPI).
geometry_msgs/Point[] waypoints
# Stamp of the frame the waypoints were defined on (from PlanVisualPath.stamp): the
# projector looks up the robot pose at this time to ground the image markers into
# odom. {sec: 0, nanosec: 0} uses the latest frame.
builtin_interfaces/Time stamp
---
# Result
# Success/failure is the action's terminal status (SUCCEEDED vs ABORTED) — no
# redundant `success` bool (matching PlanVisualPath / Reason). Reaching the goal (or a
# turn-only no-op with no drivable path) SUCCEEDS; a blocked/no-progress follow,
# a rejected goal, or a grounding failure ABORTS, with the reason in `message`.
string message
---
# Feedback
string state
